<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       id="PlaceholderAPI" title="PlaceholderAPI">

    <title>
        PlaceholderAPI
    </title>
    <primary-label ref="dependency-required"/>
    <chapter title="Placeholders" id="placeholders">
        <p>Honeypot supports Placeholders and even provides three as well. If you want to use custom
            placeholders, you may do so by adding them to your honeypots.yml file.
        </p>
        <chapter title="Supported Placeholders" id="supported-placeholders">
            <list>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_current_count_[type]&percnt;</code> -- This placeholder displays the count of
                    Honeypots the player has broken
                    <emphasis>this cycle</emphasis>
                    for a given <code>type</code>. Types are one of: <code>break</code>, <code>inventory_open</code>,
                    <code>inventory_interact</code>,
                    or <code>generic</code>. This will
                    <emphasis>never</emphasis>
                    be more than the trigger limit configured for that type in config.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_current_count_[type]_[playerName]&percnt;</code> -- This is the same as the
                    previous placeholder, except
                    it gets a specific player's count instead of the current player viewing/seeing it.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_lifetime_triggers&percnt;</code> -- This is the all-time total count of
                    Honeypots
                    the current player has triggered. This does not necessarily mean action was taken, but rather a
                    trigger
                    was counted against them.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_lifetime_triggers_[playerName]&percnt;</code> -- This is the same as the
                    previous placeholder, except it gets a specific player's lifetime trigger count instead of the
                    current
                    player viewing/seeing it.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_lifetime_actions&percnt;</code> -- This is the all-time total count of
                    actions
                    that have been taken against the current player. This is
                    <emphasis>only</emphasis>
                    action taken, not
                    how many Honeypots they've triggered.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_lifetime_actions_[playerName]&percnt;</code> -- This is the same as the
                    previous placeholder, except it gets a specific player's lifetime action count instead of the
                    current
                    player viewing/seeing it.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_triggers_before_action_[type]&percnt;</code> -- This placeholder displays the
                    count of triggers any given player needs to reach before action is taken against them for a given
                    <code>type</code>. Types are one of: <code>break</code>, <code>inventory_open</code>, <code>inventory_interact</code>,
                    or <code>generic</code>.
                </li>
            </list>
        </chapter>
        <chapter title="Legacy Placeholders" id="legacy-placeholders">
            <p>Honeypot's existing Placeholders are still supported, but are considered legacy and will be removed in
                the future. These placeholders only support the "blocks broken" trigger. It's recommended you use the
                new placeholders so that all triggers can be displayed.</p>
            <list>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_current_count_broken&percnt;</code> -- This placeholder displays the count of
                    Honeypots the player has
                    broken
                    <emphasis>this cycle</emphasis>
                    . This means that this value will
                    <emphasis>never</emphasis>
                    be more than <code>trigger-limits.blocks-broken</code> in
                    config.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_breaks_before_action&percnt;</code> -- This placeholder displays the value of
                    <code>trigger-limits.blocks-broken</code>.
                </li>
                <li><code>&percnt;honeypot_current_count_broken_&lt;player&gt;&percnt;</code> -- This placeholder will
                    get
                    the current amount of Honeypots
                    a specific player has broken
                    <emphasis>this cycle</emphasis>
                    . This value will
                    <emphasis>never</emphasis>
                    be more than <code>trigger-limits.blocks-broken</code> in
                    config.
                </li>
            </list>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

